'''Banyalbufar''' (from {{Langx|ar|بانيالبهار|Banyalbahar|founded by the sea}}) is the largest city in [[Cabu Verd]], an insular [[Regions of Balisca|region]] of [[Araucaria]] within [[Balisca]]. It is situated on the island of [[Alcázar (island)|Alcázar]] ("the castle") in the [[Aethiopian Ocean]]. It is home to one of the largest [[Mozbayana|Mozbayan Baliscan]] communities in Balisca, and is famous for it's {{W|Mudéjar art|Mudéjar and Neo-Mudéjar architecture}}. It has some of the best-preserved displays of the historic Ibero-Mozarabic culture, in addition to containing notable examples of {{W|Moorish Revival architecture}}.

